			"notes": "# Changelog\nDetecting Emissives and Trimming armor\n### Changes:\n- Added Emission Detector Enchantment\n\t- Renamed Geiger Finder to Emission Detector\n\t- Changed the sound of ticking to Bit\n\t- Detects emissive materials near the player\n\t- The closer you get to emissive material the faster its sound ticks\n\t- Applied to Helmets\n\t- Can be obtained through Librarians or Enchanting Table\n\t- Only detects Reptianium for now\n- Reptianium armor is now trimmable\n\n---\n### Fixed Bugs:\n- Fixed Forge crashing on startup due to registering Trades before Items\n- Fixed Geiger Finder (now Emission Detector) ticking sound from getting buggy when near multiple Radioactive Materials (from v0.0.7-Alpha and prior)\n\n---\n\n### Known Issues:\nCurrently no known issues, If you encounter an issue, please report it through the GitHub Issue Tracker\n\n---\n### Notes:\n- NAI Additions version is `0.1.1-Alpha`\n- I might keep the Emission Detector ticking sound to Bit, as I don't have any other good sound\n- Thanks to the way Mojang made trimmable armor, I could copy and paste the 45 JSON files of Diamond armor and replace Diamond with Reptianium\n---\nP.S.: I'm making this project for fun! And also to learn Java, It might not get updated or maintained frequently, But I will try to not abandon it."
